1549..1622 Comment "/// The winding number into the native integers, a fold that rests on the"
1623..1680 Comment "/// native model\'s laws. At `Loop(Unloop(x))` it computes"
1681..1752 Comment "/// `turn(unturn(native_wind(x)))`, which conversion does not reduce to"
1753..1829 Comment "/// `native_wind(x)` on a variable; the law `turnUnturn` states exactly that"
1830..1906 Comment "/// path, so `respects` names it for the first rule and `unturnTurn` for the"
1907..1981 Comment "/// second. The loop arms call the model\'s operations rather than spelling"
1982..2060 Comment "/// `n + 1`, so each side the rule relates is the law\'s own endpoint. The fold"
2061..2103 Comment "/// checks and owes what its two laws owe."
2104..2106 Other "@["
